  "instance_name": "forced_religious_indoctrination_stereotype",
  "label": "Stereotype of forced religious indoctrination",
  "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that religious institutions impose beliefs on children, which is often used in secular or anti-religious discourse to criticize organized religion. This stereotype frames religious upbringing as coercive or unnatural, implying that true belief must be freely chosen, not taught or instilled. The visual of children carrying crosses is used to evoke this stereotype, even though the image may not depict actual religious indoctrination.",
